# Instruction fidelity

## Mode (check first)
- **Suggest / explain / plan / review / why / suggestion** → **words only. No repo edits.**
- **Do / go / implement / fix** (scoped ask) → code or doc edits **only after** STOP block below.

- **`push to git all` / `push to git all ok` / `push to git all good`** → add all changed files (skip secrets), commit (`ok`/`good` in message if said), push; update STATUS + MAP if needed; reply in plain English what changed in each of those two docs + push result.

## STOP (before any repo edit)
Every file is protected. Post in chat **before** Write / StrReplace / Delete:

1. **Quote the ask** — one line.
2. **`Go — <task>`** + **Files:** (paths) + **Out:** (excluded) — else **NONE**.

**Not approval:** suggest/explain alone, silence, frustration. Plain `push to git` / `commit local` without **all** = agent picks files; no automatic STATUS/MAP sync.

Edited without approval → say so, offer revert.

## After edits
One short block per ask: what changed, what you ran, pass/fail, **UNCONFIRMED** if not seen on screen.

## Always-on
- **Say = do** — u must only claim outcomes you verified.
- Git, verify, process, code–doc, tests, SmartBeads hooks → `GPT_PROJECT_RULES_01P.md`.
